Major live-streaming events are commonly assumed to generate traffic surges observable across diverse network vantage points. We challenge this assumption by conducting a measurement study during UEFA EURO 2024, utilizing traffic statistics from various European IXPs and a research network. Most IXPs show no notable traffic peaks during match broadcasts, while the clearest signal emerges at the CDN peering link within a research network. We show that vantage point selection can be the decisive factor between reporting a result or observing nothing at all.